"The Software" means everything in this repository: the skill, the style recipes, the references, the
scripts, assets/print.js, assets/starter.html and the documentation. "Your work" means the designs,
images, pages, prints, videos and other output you make by running the Software, and any recipe you
write yourself from styles/_template.md.

The Software is source available, not open source. You may read it and use it to make your own work.
You may not copy it, share it, sell it or rebuild it.

1. What you may do

   a. Read and study the Software.
   b. Download, install and run the Software, unmodified, on computers you own or control, to make
      your work. This includes installing it as a Claude Code plugin or skill for an AI agent that you
      direct.
   c. Copy assets/print.js and assets/starter.html into your own design projects, as the skill directs,
      change those copies as your project needs, and ship them inside your work (for example in a
      poster's source file or a client's web page). You may not offer print.js on its own, as a
      library, package or download.
   d. Write your own recipes with styles/_template.md. Recipes you write are yours.
   e. Use, publish and sell your work, for personal or commercial projects, including work for your own
      clients, with no fee. You own your work. Credit ("Art direction with idra-taste") is welcome but
      not required.

2. What you may not do

   a. Except as section 1 allows, copy, share, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, rent or lend the
      Software or any substantial part of it, in source or any other form. This includes the style
      recipes and references, alone or as a collection.
   b. Modify the Software, or make, share or publish modified versions of it or works based on it. You
      may make small private changes needed to run it on your own computers, as long as you never share
      them. Your project copies under section 1c and your own recipes are not affected by this.
   c. Offer the Software, or anything built with it, to others as a product or service: for example a
      hosted design tool, an API, an app, a style or template pack, or a prompt library. Making work for
      your own clients is allowed (section 1e).
   d. Recreate the Software: use its recipes, references, code or skill to build, or to help anyone
      build, a skill, plugin, style library, tool or service that does the same job as the Software or
      competes with it.
   e. Use the Software or its documentation to train or fine-tune a machine learning model, or put them
      in a dataset.
   f. Remove or change this licence or the copyright notices.
   g. Use the names IDRA or idra-taste, or the IDRA logo, to name or promote your own product. You may
      say that a piece was made with idra-taste.

3. Third-party parts

   idra-taste bundles no code or fonts from other projects. The Risograph ink names and hex values
   quoted in the recipes come from the riso-colors data (MIT), and the plugins, libraries and fonts the
   Software installs or loads keep their own licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY.md. Nothing in this licence
   limits what those terms allow for them.

4. GitHub

   This repository is public on GitHub. GitHub's Terms of Service let GitHub users view it and fork it
   on GitHub. A fork carries this licence with it and gives no other rights.

5. Ending

   If you break this licence, your permission ends automatically. If you put things right within 30
   days of being told, your permission comes back. Work you made while your permission was in place
   stays yours.

6. Other uses

